message: "If you use SURGITOME in teaching, research or publications, please cite it as below."
title: "SURGITOME — interactive 3D postoperative gastrointestinal anatomy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Spychalski
    given-names: Piotr
    email: piotr.spychalski@gumed.edu.pl
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7111-4660"
    affiliation: "Department of Surgical Oncology, Transplant Surgery and General Surgery, Medical University of Gdańsk (Gdański Uniwersytet Medyczny), Gdańsk, Poland"
version: "2026.9.26"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
url: "https://bit.ly/surgitome"
abstract: >-
  SURGITOME is an interactive, schematic 3D atlas of postoperative gastrointestinal anatomy
  created by Piotr Spychalski, MD, PhD, colorectal surgeon at the Medical University of Gdańsk.
  For 23 procedures (47 variants) in oesophageal, gastric, bariatric, hepatopancreatobiliary,
  small-bowel and colorectal surgery it shows the extent of resection, animated stapled and
  hand-sewn anastomoses, first-person postoperative endoscopy with route choice at forks, and
  schematic cross-sectional CT. Intended for medical students, physicians of other specialties
  (endoscopists, radiologists), surgical trainees and for explaining the extent of resection to patients.
keywords:
  - postoperative anatomy
  - colorectal surgery
  - gastrointestinal surgery
  - surgical anastomosis
  - surgical education
  - endoscopy after surgery
  - 3D anatomy
  - medical education
